+ * its symbol when the image exports one). The stacks the kernel prints (ustacks=) stop at sixteen
+ * frames and know no names, and 3 threads is too little to tell an idle run loop from a wait: this
+ * says what each thread stands in, so the one that keeps the window server from the first frame is
+ * named. The run loop of the main thread is watched from here as well: "woke N ms ago" tells whether
+ * the main thread is alive at all.
